WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:05.100
We have to maybe convince ourselves
that this is what we want to be doing.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.570
This is fun for us.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:07.770
This is enjoyable.

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:09.720
Hi there, Steve Kaufman here.

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:14.430
Today I want to talk about how to stay
motivated when you're learning a language.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:17.880
Remember, if you enjoy these
videos, please subscribe.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:23.160
And if you follow these podcasts
on Spotify or Apple Podcasts or

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:24.780
elsewhere, please leave a review.

00:00:25.785 --> 00:00:28.905
Um, so motivation, it
comes up all the time.

00:00:28.935 --> 00:00:33.615
We all know that to be
successful in anything it helps

00:00:33.615 --> 00:00:35.745
to be genuinely motivated.

00:00:36.345 --> 00:00:39.945
And we also know that we
are more motivated at some

00:00:39.945 --> 00:00:41.505
times and at other times.

00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:46.185
And so even in learning a language,
we can be very molded, motivated

00:00:46.185 --> 00:00:47.775
initially for whatever reason.

00:00:48.105 --> 00:00:50.235
And then we go through periods
where we're not motivated.

00:00:50.445 --> 00:00:51.915
So how do we stay motivated?

00:00:52.335 --> 00:00:57.210
Well, First of all, let's say that we
can't be equally motivated all the time.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:59.700
So at times your motivation will flag.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:05.250
However, I think the first thing about
motivation is to have a clear goal.

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:07.740
Why are you learning this language?

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:08.400
All right.

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:12.750
Is it because you want to communicate
with your in-laws in the old country?

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.510
Uh, is it because you need it for a job?

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.870
Is it because you're interested
in some aspect of the culture?

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:22.160
Or you have a friend, uh,
or you want to travel.

00:01:22.455 --> 00:01:25.635
You know, make sure you
have some clear goal.

00:01:25.695 --> 00:01:28.725
Maybe you just want to learn the
language so you can show off in front

00:01:28.725 --> 00:01:31.265
of others, uh, perfectly legitimate.

00:01:31.745 --> 00:01:36.275
Uh, maybe you want to learn a language
because it's an improvement activity

00:01:36.335 --> 00:01:40.265
and we all know that, you know, as
human beings, if we can learn, if we

00:01:40.265 --> 00:01:44.615
can learn, if we can improve ourselves,
it gives us a sense of satisfaction.

00:01:44.615 --> 00:01:47.345
It gets the, I dunno,
endorphins, adrenaline or

00:01:47.345 --> 00:01:48.515
something, working in the brain.

00:01:48.515 --> 00:01:49.065
We like that.

00:01:49.065 --> 00:01:51.215
The brain likes that
the sense of, of attack.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:54.119
And that sense of acquiring knowledge.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:57.660
And there's a great sense of
achievement and satisfaction,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:00.270
uh, which, which comes from that.

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:04.679
And those are all legitimate reasons,
goals for learning a language.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:08.160
And I could probably, I'm sure
that people out there have other

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:10.169
goals that are also legitimate.

00:02:10.169 --> 00:02:15.690
Any goal that motivates you to
learn is, is, is important to have.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.170
So I think a big part of
motivation is the goal.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.760
And when your motivation flags you got
to remind yourself of why you're doing

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.530
it, remind yourself of why this is
important to you, to learn this language.

00:02:28.710 --> 00:02:32.520
And of course, if it's no longer
important, then maybe you should stop for

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.090
a while until you get that itch again,
you know, I want to learn this language.

00:02:36.270 --> 00:02:40.590
So a big part of motivation
is, is the goal, the why.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.820
Another big part of motivation
is the process itself.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.270
And I often say, you know,
the process is the reward.

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:54.570
Uh, if you can enjoy the process
of learning a language, then you're

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:58.709
not, you're less concerned about how
quickly you're improving, because

00:02:58.709 --> 00:03:03.090
you're enjoying hearing the sounds
of the language, discovering new

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.220
words, new ways of saying things.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:09.690
Uh, you're enjoying the fact that you
understand things now that you didn't

00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:11.790
understand three or six months earlier.

00:03:11.970 --> 00:03:16.019
You're not frustrated by the
fact that you don't understand.

00:03:17.024 --> 00:03:22.334
So the, the, the whole, the process
itself, uh, gives you a sense of

00:03:22.334 --> 00:03:23.685
achievement, a sense of enjoyment.

00:03:24.584 --> 00:03:28.155
So therefore you have to look for
ways to make that process enjoyable.

00:03:28.484 --> 00:03:32.864
I've talked about mixing in repetition,
which is easier, or, you know, a lot

00:03:32.864 --> 00:03:36.285
of the content, and you're focusing
in on some aspects, some structures

00:03:36.285 --> 00:03:40.515
in the language, or some ways in which
words change in the language, some

00:03:40.515 --> 00:03:42.195
aspects of grammar in the language.

00:03:42.435 --> 00:03:47.370
So listening to repetitious material
can be enjoyable, but at the same

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:53.160
time, you want to find enjoyable
content, uh, things of interest to you.

00:03:53.459 --> 00:03:56.160
So that again, the
process becomes enjoyable.

00:03:56.865 --> 00:04:01.484
Uh, you know, just as an aside, uh,
on Twitter, I sometimes comment on

00:04:01.484 --> 00:04:03.045
different tweets that come my way.

00:04:03.045 --> 00:04:08.475
And some person had tweeted that, uh,
you know, he's 16 and jobs, any job

00:04:08.505 --> 00:04:12.675
he's had is boring and he only gets a
few weeks off and he's got, that's all

00:04:12.675 --> 00:04:14.355
he's got to look forward to in his life.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:18.315
And I said, well, you know,
with an attitude like that, you

00:04:18.325 --> 00:04:19.605
probably better to quit the job.

00:04:19.635 --> 00:04:22.875
If you, if you think the job is
genuinely pointless, find another

00:04:22.915 --> 00:04:27.525
job, uh, because even in work, if
you can find a way to enjoy the

00:04:27.525 --> 00:04:29.835
process, you will be more successful.

00:04:30.344 --> 00:04:35.025
Uh, and of course that brought an
avalanche of Twitter comments from

00:04:35.055 --> 00:04:39.354
people who were, I don't know, communist
or whatever they were, jobs are all

00:04:39.375 --> 00:04:42.015
bad and the boss gets all the money.

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:46.664
We make useless stuff that only goes
to the rich and all this other stuff.

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:49.350
And nobody enjoys their work.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:52.170
And you obviously were in a
position of power, you old

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:54.210
white man boomer or whatever.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.060
I don't believe that.

00:04:57.090 --> 00:04:59.820
When I go to a restaurant,
I have the impression that

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:01.870
the server enjoys serving me.

00:05:02.294 --> 00:05:04.125
Uh, I have worked in factories.

00:05:04.125 --> 00:05:09.255
I worked, okay I wasn't a permanent
laborer there, but I have worked together

00:05:09.255 --> 00:05:12.344
with people in factories for weeks on end.

00:05:12.344 --> 00:05:16.424
I've also been part of the management
team and a majority of people actually

00:05:16.424 --> 00:05:22.184
enjoy what they do, and those who do enjoy
what they do, they do better, uh, because

00:05:22.184 --> 00:05:23.895
it's not just eight hours of drudgery.

00:05:24.044 --> 00:05:27.405
Not to mention the fact that, you
know, it's a social environment where

00:05:27.405 --> 00:05:30.575
they're together with their buddies and
it's an important part of their life.

00:05:30.975 --> 00:05:36.305
As we go through life, no matter what our
activity is, you know, we have some...

00:05:36.355 --> 00:05:40.475
some ability to control how
we feel about that activity.

00:05:40.685 --> 00:05:43.715
We can decide that we're going
to enjoy that activity or,

00:05:43.745 --> 00:05:45.275
or not enjoy that activity.

00:05:45.935 --> 00:05:50.945
And it's not obvious that a, you know,
a very wealthy person who's have nothing

00:05:50.945 --> 00:05:55.205
but the best of everything to eat and the
biggest home is enjoying his life more

00:05:55.325 --> 00:05:59.655
than someone who has a simpler life but
has lots of interests, lots of friends

00:05:59.655 --> 00:06:01.935
and family and relationships and stuff.

00:06:02.565 --> 00:06:04.335
So it's up to it up to us.

00:06:04.395 --> 00:06:07.755
And so that's, sorry for the
digression, but I think the same

00:06:07.755 --> 00:06:10.005
is true in our language learning.

00:06:10.545 --> 00:06:15.435
We have to maybe convince ourselves
that this is what we want to be doing.

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:16.905
This is fun for us.

00:06:16.905 --> 00:06:18.105
This is enjoyable.

00:06:18.615 --> 00:06:25.895
So if we have these goals and at the
same time we enjoy the process, we find

00:06:25.895 --> 00:06:30.695
things that are enjoyable to do, or we
persuade ourselves that this is worthwhile

00:06:30.695 --> 00:06:35.224
doing, this is what I want to be doing
now, so that the process is enjoyable.

00:06:35.435 --> 00:06:37.955
All of these things are motivating.

00:06:38.465 --> 00:06:43.135
Uh, if we are frustrated by the
difficulties, frustrated by our obvious,

00:06:43.585 --> 00:06:49.275
uh, you know, problems in the language,
which are part and parcel of learning it,

00:06:49.275 --> 00:06:52.665
because if we knew the language and made
no mistakes and understood everything,

00:06:52.665 --> 00:06:53.685
then we wouldn't need to learn it.

00:06:53.685 --> 00:06:57.105
So, because we're learning it, we are
in fact encountering these difficulties,

00:06:57.255 --> 00:07:02.685
but we can find a way to enjoy these
difficulties if we set our minds to it.

00:07:03.135 --> 00:07:07.725
So those are sort of my main
thoughts on, on motivation.

00:07:08.045 --> 00:07:12.870
Another thing that comes up from time
to time, if you have been studying the

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.620
same bit of content and you kind of think
you should be doing this content because

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:20.219
it's the next level of difficulty, but
you're not really interested in the

00:07:20.219 --> 00:07:24.510
content, find something else because
there's a tremendous difference.

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.930
If we're interested, like let's say
that it's something in the language

00:07:27.930 --> 00:07:31.440
you're learning and it relates to your
job or relates to a sport that you're

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:33.510
interested in, skiing or something.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.950
And all of a sudden it's interesting.

00:07:35.159 --> 00:07:39.575
I mean, that level of focus that
we can achieve when we have content

00:07:39.575 --> 00:07:43.925
that's genuinely interesting, you
know, is, is so much stronger.

00:07:43.925 --> 00:07:47.925
That pull, the resonance is so much
stronger than if we're studying

00:07:47.945 --> 00:07:50.855
something that we feel we should
study and we're kind of pushing

00:07:50.855 --> 00:07:52.115
ourselves and forcing ourselves.

00:07:52.115 --> 00:07:57.485
So make sure in order to maintain
motivation, motivation that you work

00:07:57.485 --> 00:08:03.305
with content that has some value to you
either because, and I find myself very

00:08:03.305 --> 00:08:06.755
motivated to listen to my mini stories
over and over again, but at the same

00:08:06.755 --> 00:08:11.340
time find things that are interesting, so
that all of a sudden from being somewhat

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:15.330
passive and I should really do this, you
all of a sudden, wow, I'm interested in

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:19.680
this and you'll see that you won't even
notice that you're learning the language.

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:20.520
You won't even notice it.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:24.270
The language is washing over your
brain because you're pursuing something

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.710
there that's of interest to you.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.120
And that helps with motivation.

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:27.900
Okay.

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:28.980
Thank you for listening.

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:29.730
Bye for now.

